              <h2>What the system does and why teams depended on it</h2>
              <p>SEOOnDemand is an AI platform built for SEO agencies and content operations teams managing multiple websites. The product was designed to turn ranking signals and analytics data into a repeatable content pipeline instead of manual topic planning and publishing work.</p>
              <p>From an engineering perspective, the system had to support multi-site campaign workflows, queued AI generation, and editorial visibility without making the product slow or brittle. That made it a production platform with real operational demands rather than a portfolio demo.</p>
            </article>
            <article class="content-panel">
              <span class="section-kicker">Business Challenge</span>
              <h2>What had to improve for the product to scale cleanly</h2>
              <p>The core business challenge was delivering a product that could serve AI content automation and marketing operations use cases while still remaining easy for operators to trust and use every day.</p>
              <p>The client wanted a stronger service margin by converting SEO delivery into software-supported, data-driven operations rather than manual agency labor.</p>
            </article>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

